-- <msg:5> helper (html)
   | <!-- codex-helper-outbox:<marker> --><p><strong>🔧 Helper:</strong></p>
   | <p><strong>🔔 Workflow webhook setup</strong></p>
   | <p>Use this to send notification cards when Codex finishes, restarts, or needs your attention.</p>
   | <p>Step 1: Open Workflows here<br>
   | In this Control chat, click the <code>+</code> button at the lower right of the message box, then choose <code>Workflow</code>.</p>
   | <p>Step 2: Pick exactly this Workflow template<br>
   | Search <code>webhook</code>, then choose exactly: <strong>Send webhook alerts to a chat</strong></p>
   | <p>Step 3: Confirm the target chat<br>
   | Keep the target set to this Control chat:<br>
   | 🏠 Codex Control - e2ehost<br>
   | Chat ID: <code><chat:1></code></p>
   | <p>Step 4: Create the Workflow and copy the URL<br>
   | Click <code>Next</code> / <code>Add workflow</code>. Teams will show a webhook URL; copy it.</p>
   | <p>Step 5: Send this here<br>
   | <code>helper webhook &lt;paste-url&gt;</code><br>
   | If Teams turns the pasted URL into a shortened hyperlink, paste the full URL as plain text instead.</p>
   | <p>Need the Microsoft walkthrough? Open <a href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/create-incoming-webhooks-with-workflows-for-microsoft-teams-<uuid:1>">Teams webhook setup guide</a> (https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/create-incoming-webhooks-with-workflows-for-microsoft-teams-<uuid:1>).</p>
   | <p>Note: Microsoft does not provide a reliable one-click link that pre-fills every workflow field and returns the generated webhook URL.</p>
